@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] deployment-preserves-local-work
The updater MUST refuse staged or unstaged tracked deployment edits without discarding
them. Dependency installation MUST NOT rewrite the deployment's editor-skill lockfile.
Source: Tavi, 21 Oct 2026, "fix all the things you mentioned", after local release edits
blocked every fast-forward update.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] deployment-failures-are-visible
A failed APK publish or attempted version downgrade MUST fail the updater service. An APK
publish failure MUST be retried on the next invocation even when the server revision has
already deployed. A failed server build MUST leave the previous server running.
Source: Tavi, 21 Oct 2026, "fix all the things you mentioned" in the stale APK investigation.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] deployment-preserves-active-ai
Automatic deployment MUST defer while AI work, pending admission or follow-up registration
is active. The running backend MUST atomically fence new admissions before accepting an
idle shutdown. Missing idle-update support MUST defer rather than fall back to cancelling
work. After shutdown the updater MUST ensure the replacement is started, never restart a
replacement which may already have accepted new work. Source: Tavi, 21 Oct 2026,
"Resolve all reviews and merge those PRs", active-work deployment review.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] deployment-consumes-the-verified-release-track
Main MUST be a fast integration branch and MUST NOT automatically restart the server
or publish an APK. Both the current updater and a captured legacy main-tracking
installed updater MUST fail before building or restarting unverified main source.
Publication MUST require the exact remote release commit and successful complete
release checks; unavailable evidence MUST preserve the previous running release.
Changing source defaults MUST NOT claim that an installed script or live timer was
migrated. Source: Tavi's 22 Oct 2026 fast-main and protected-release decision.
